            <div xml:id="d465">

                <pb facs="0582" n="572" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg572"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893–50 Recovery/6–2548: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-06-25T16:00:00+09:00">June 25, 1948—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 25—8:09 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1149. In light Cleveland–Gilpatric telephone conversation and discussion with ECA
                    Mission here June 25, Embassy has agreed best wording article IV, paragraph 4 is
                    first sentence recommended for paragraph 4 in <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Toeca</hi> 31 of June 11 and so presented in <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> today. Embassy likewise now supports ECA strong desire
                    leave article VII, paragraph 5, unchanged, and accordingly has not submitted NAC
                    suggestion paragraph 5 to Foreign Office. Lapham will telegraph ECA from
                    Shanghai detailed supporting views.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 1149, repeated Shanghai 525.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
